%% DM26-0670

%% What an agent asks the credentials agent over Cassini, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/credentials-agent-architecture.md, credentials-policy.md). The custodian's
%% own requests are general/workload_certificate_issuance and multi_instance_workload. Requests relayed by the observer are judged as the observer.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Crypto as An agent's CryptoActor
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Gate as Credentials agent<br/>(request gate)
    participant H as Its handler
    participant Ledger as Ledger

    Crypto-)Bk: a request on its topic, with share_identity
    Bk-)Gate: the request, published_by stamped by the broker
    Gate->>Gate: a topic it serves, a stamped publisher, a certificate on record
    Gate->>Gate: Cedar: Action request on Request TOPIC. Where it is silent, the floor:<br/>the requester publishes this topic in the authority model
    Note over Gate: Refused here: a warning and a drop, with no reply and no record. The asker waits out its timeout
    Gate->>H: admitted

    alt EscrowKeyRequest
        H-->>Crypto: the credentials agent's own public key. Cached by the asker
    else AgentEscrowKeyRequest (EncryptForRecipient, and the observer's /agent-escrow-key)
        H->>Ledger: CheckAgentEscrowKey
        H-->>Crypto: Found { public key, certificate } or NotFound. The asker believes it only if the certificate holds
    else StoreSecret
        H->>H: a publisher, a valid name and labels, a certificate on record
        H->>H: Cedar: Action store on Secret NAME. Where it is silent or absent,<br/>the floor: its own namespace only. Forbidden: PolicyDenied
        H->>H: sealed to the current escrow key, else WrongEscrowKey
        H->>Ledger: StoreSecret: another identity's name is NameTaken, its own with other labels LabelsChanged
        Ledger->>Ledger: append SecretStored.<br/>Storing it again unchanged<br/>is how a restart closes its loop
        H-->>Crypto: Stored, or the refusal
    else RetrieveSecret
        H->>H: a publisher, a valid name that is not an escrow keypair, a certificate on record
        H->>H: Cedar: Action retrieve on Secret NAME, with no floor: anything but Allow is Denied
        H->>Ledger: the requester's escrow certificate, then the secret
        H->>H: open it, seal it to the requester's escrow key. No record is written
        H-->>Crypto: Found, NotFound, Denied or Failed
        Crypto->>Crypto: a credential's own record<br/>is refused here, IsACredential
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Crypto,Ledger: BUILT, WITH NO CALLER, AND NOT WORKING: DecryptOnBehalfOf. No CryptoMessage asks, nothing in the catalog publishes its topic, so the floor<br/>refuses it and only a Cedar permit could admit it. It seals to the requester's client certificate read as RSA, and a workload's client key<br/>is Ed25519 or P-256: a real requester would get Failed after policy allows. The retrieve path's lookup and parser are the model for a fix
    Gate->>H: credentials-decrypt-on-behalf-of-requests
    H->>H: Cedar: Action decrypt on the caller's resource_id, Allow only
    H-->>Crypto: Allowed, Denied, Refused or Failed
    end
